- Affected when the player is equipping, unequipping, dropping, stowing, retrieving,
  drinking, throwing, trading, giving, receiving, looting, purchasing, crafting,
  loading, or repairing physical items and gear.
- Crafting always affects inventory — the resulting item is added regardless of whether
  a Craft check is needed. needs_mechanics depends on whether crafting requires a roll.
- Acquiring items through looting, purchasing, or receiving as rewards affects inventory.
- Giving or trading items to NPCs affects inventory — the item leaves the player's possession.
- Dropping or discarding an item affects inventory.
- Using a consumable (potion, alchemist's fire, scroll, holy water) affects inventory
  — the item is expended. needs_mechanics: false unless activation requires a roll
  (Use Magic Device for scrolls/wands).
- Drawing or sheathing a weapon in combat is a combat action, NOT inventory, unless
  the player is explicitly swapping loadouts between scenes.
- needs_mechanics: false for most item management. needs_mechanics: true for identification,
  crafting with a Craft check, or activating items requiring Use Magic Device.